  <h2>About energy procurement</h2>
  <p>
    Energy-sector tenders are issued by Eskom (transmission build-out, generation refurbishment), the
    Department of Mineral Resources and Energy, the IPP Office (REIPPPP and battery procurement), municipal
    distribution utilities, and a growing number of public buildings procuring solar PV and storage under
    their own energy resilience programmes. The just-energy-transition pipeline in Mpumalanga adds
    decommissioning and repurposing tenders.
  </p>

  <h2>Detailed sector hub — coming soon</h2>
  <p>
    We're building a detailed energy-sector hub covering Eskom transmission tenders, IPP and balance-of-plant
    procurement, municipal embedded generation, energy efficiency retrofits, and the JET-tied programmes.
    We'll also cover the compliance environment — NERSA licensing, OEM accreditations, electrical
    contractor registration, and the safety regime for high-voltage work. Join the waitlist below.
  </p>

  <p>
    In the meantime, the
    <a href="https://www.etenders.gov.za" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">eTenders Publication Portal</a>
    lists current energy-sector tenders. Eskom-specific procurement also goes through the
    <a href="https://tenderbulletin.eskom.co.za" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Eskom Tender Bulletin</a>.
  </p>
</TenderHubLayout>
